      "writtenOn": "2022-06-15T17:15:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this would be expected.\n\nI.e., if an updateConfiguration is in-progress, if a second updateConfiguration call is made, it will abort the first one (and send a callback for the first one letting it know).\n\nThere is actually a test for this as well if helpful (in this patch it is on EthernetNetworkFactoryTest.java on l.640) named testUpdateInterfaceCallsListenerCorrectlyOnConcurrentRequests.\n\nYeah, they are a bit confusing but I actually think you\u0027re suggestion to move the  maybeSendNetworkManagementCallbackForAbort() into stop() in some ways make it less confusing; any time you stop() the interface, if an update is in progress, a them a callback is sent. \n\nThinking about it like that seems to make it simpler (at least IMO).",
